  "instructions": [
    "Peel and finely chop the onion, grate the ginger and garlic, cut the cauliflower into small florets, and drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
    "Put the oil in a large pan on a medium heat, add the cumin seeds and fry for 30 seconds. Add the onion and cook on medium-low, stirring, for 10 minutes, until golden brown. Add the ginger, garlic, cumin, coriander, turmeric, chilli and salt, turn the heat to low and stir-fry for 2 minutes.",
    "Stir in the coconut milk, add the cauliflower and chickpeas and bring to the boil. Simmer for 15 minutes, until the cauliflower is just cooked. Add the spinach and cook for 2 more minutes, until wilted.",
    "Turn off the heat and leave for 10 minutes, then add the lime juice, taste and adjust the salt. Serve with rice or flatbreads."
  ],
